 {:seon.task/name "a-commit-of-no-text-starts-no-round"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by Optimization (2026-11-10, task seon.writer/a-main-notice-says-whether-program-content-moved). seon.vector/vectors-proc runs a round at every main commit notice (seon.vector/round: the commit's db made, one datoms-diff since the last round's commit, due's seeks), though nearly every commit is records (an agent's status per request) or its own embedding write, which hold no text. The notice already carries the commit's resolved datoms (:ops), as the test service and the fork server read them (seon.program/moves-program?). Cut: a notice whose :ops hold no datom of a text attribute (seon.vector/texts), with nothing owed and the proc caught up, starts no round; the next round's diff from the last commit it scanned still finds every text since. The proc's tests build notices without :ops (vector-test's note): they must carry the commit's ops, as the writer's do. Estimate first: what a round costs on a records-only commit on a 2,931-form main (n = the datoms since the last round; expected the diff and an at-commit, under 1 ms), and how often it runs (every request). Proof: seon.vector-test/a-commit-of-no-text-starts-no-round (a status-only notice: no round, no read; a form's notice: a round)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.vector-test/a-commit-of-no-text-starts-no-round}}
